   "stem": {
      "text": "Let r(x) = (x + 2) / (x^3 - 9x). State the intervals on which r is continuous and give a reason. On how many separate maximal intervals is r continuous?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Factor the denominator as x(x - 3)(x + 3), which is zero at x = -3, x = 0 and x = 3, and the numerator never cancels any of these factors.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            "x",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               3
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "A rational function is continuous at every input of its domain. Its domain is every real x except -3, 0 and 3.",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "r is continuous on (-infinity, -3), (-3, 0), (0, 3) and (3, infinity), all open at the excluded inputs.",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Those are four separate maximal intervals.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
